.\" Distro-authored man page for the Fedora pidp8i package.
.\" Candidate for upstreaming to the PiDP-8/I project.
.TH PIDP8I-TEST 1 "November 21, 2026" "PiDP-8/I" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pidp8i-test \- PiDP-8/I front-panel GPIO self-test
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pidp8i-test
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pidp8i-test
walks the PiDP-8/I front panel: it drives the lamps and reads back the
switch matrix over the Raspberry Pi GPIO so you can verify the panel
wiring and the GPIO pin-assignment configuration (the
.BR gpio-hog /
overlay setup) before trusting the panel to the simulator.
.PP
It needs a real cabinet: on any other machine it prints
.I "No GPIO chips found"
and exits without testing anything.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pidp8i-sim (1),
.BR scanswitch (8),
the panel-configuration notes under
.I /usr/share/doc/pidp8i/
